 "rules": [
  "Facts go into files of 10 to 25 facts each under aws-saa-book/_build/work/11-vpc-connectivity/ named facts-<lens>-NN.json (lens names: numbers, changes, behavior, decisions, faq).",
  "Every quote is copied verbatim from the saved snapshot (use search and show; use tables for table rows with their header, for example 'tables docs/vpc/latest/tgw/transit-gateway-quotas --index 2'). Never paraphrase inside a quote. A display of a fact without numbers is a verbatim phrase of at most 8 words from the quote.",
  "The quote must carry every clause, scope, condition and exception of the claim on its own. When the condition stands in the next sentence (for example 'even if you intend to use only the non-overlapping CIDR blocks', 'inbound rules only', 'only supported for VPC attachments', 'same Region'), include that sentence in the quote; otherwise narrow the claim. A universal claim (only, always, never, cannot) with a nearby exception must quote the exception or be narrowed.",
  "Fact namespace by service key: vpc-peering-*, tgw-* (service key transit-gateway), vpce-* (service key vpc-endpoints), privatelink-*. Change facts use <prefix>-change-*. FAQ facts use <prefix>-faq-*. Comparison facts sit with the service they decide for (for example privatelink-vs-peering-*). Before adding, run 'python3 aws-saa-book/tools/saa.py facts list' for the ids in each item's reuse_candidates and for the chapter 10 namespace vpc-*; reuse an existing verified or mech-pass fact instead of duplicating it, and list it in your miner note against the demand id.",
  "A demand item that the pages cannot answer is reported as not-found in the miner note with what was searched; never answer from memory. A demand item whose question starts with 'Hypothesis' is a research claim to test, not a fact to confirm. Items tagged callvale ask which facts ground the story's decision; if no sentence grounds a stated trade-off, report not-found so the writer changes the reason.",
  "All pages below are in the corpus (fetched or cached by plan-11 on 2026-10-13). A page outside this list is fetched with 'python3 aws-saa-book/tools/saa.py fetch <url>' before it is quoted. Pages in brief.v0.json fetch_failures are blocked by robots.txt or unusable; use the document-history page or other page named in each reason instead.",
  "Not examinable yet: anything GA after 2026-07-15 (Transit Gateway Policy-Based Routing, PrivateLink tunnel endpoints). Record such a change fact with its date so the writer can label it; never let it replace the current examinable value in a numbers fact.",
  "Pricing: dimensions first. A dollar amount is recorded only as the page prints it, quoted with its row and header, and only where a demand item asks for it.",
  "Out of scope as answers: AWS App Mesh, Transit VPC as a recommended design (quote it only as the older pattern). Site-to-Site VPN and Direct Connect details belong to chapter 12; here quote only how they attach to a transit gateway."
 ],
 "lens_instructions": {
  "numbers+changes": "Limits, defaults, sizes, bandwidth, MTU and pricing dimensions, then change items. Use 'tables' on the three quotas pages (peering, transit-gateway-quotas, vpc-limits-endpoints) and adopt rows with their header; each value is its own fact (and the 'Adjustable' column when it states a maximum such as 'up to 125'). Quote bulleted considerations (endpoint bandwidth, MTU) one bullet per fact. Change items: date, old value where a page states it, new value, pointer to the current-truth fact; quote the document-history row (tables on the history page) or the What's New snapshot, never the feed summary. Mark items GA after 2026-07-15 as not examinable yet. Two files minimum: facts-numbers-NN.json and facts-changes-NN.json.",
  "behavior+decisions": "Can, cannot, only, by default, what happens when. One quoted sentence (plus its condition sentence) per claim; where a page gives a list of limitations (VPC peering limitations, gateway endpoint considerations, security group referencing limitations, ECMP rules, appliance mode), make one fact per list item. Work in the three batches given; write behavior-a first. Decisions: quote the whitepapers, decision guide and Well-Architected pages for every comparison (peering vs Transit Gateway vs PrivateLink; gateway vs interface vs GWLB endpoint; endpoints vs NAT gateway for cost; centralized egress and centralized endpoints trade-offs; VPC sharing, Cloud WAN, VPC Lattice, transit VPC as neighbours), the Callvale items (tagged callvale), and one quote each from the two case studies (Carrier, Resilience).",
  "faq": "Verbatim FAQ answers for the FAQ quick-fire section (medium template: 5 shipped; mine 12 to 16 for choice) from the three FAQ pages. Prefer short answers that settle a question in one or two sentences; record the question text exactly as the FAQ prints it. Many VPC FAQ peering answers already exist as facts in vpc-peering.jsonl and privatelink.jsonl: reuse them, add only the missing ones. Skip the '[] NA' rows (page noise)."
 },
